# .gitignore — PUBLIC governance repository
#
# Two jobs. First, keep build and cache artifacts out of a repo that is meant to be
# readable source. Second, and more important: make it IMPOSSIBLE to commit a
# machine-local governance config by accident.
#
# The invariant these rules protect (see README.md "Placeholder convention"):
#   a TRACKED file carries a placeholder or an env lookup;
#   the REAL value lives in a machine-local, gitignored config and is never synced.
#
# check-no-pii.sh is the gate that catches a real value that slips into a tracked file.
# The rules below are the belt to that scanner's braces: they stop the whole config file
# from being staged in the first place.

# --- Machine-local governance config — NEVER commit these -------------------
# Each one is the designated home for a real value that a tracked file only
# references by placeholder or env lookup.
.governance-local.env
.governance-mirrors
.wa-bridge.json
.pii-names

# Same files wherever they land in the tree, not just at the root.
**/.governance-local.env
**/.governance-mirrors
**/.wa-bridge.json
**/.pii-names

# --- Secrets and environment ------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
creds.json

# --- Language and build caches ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
.npm/

# --- OS cruft ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Editor / IDE -----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Logs, backups and scratch ----------------------------------------------
*.log
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
tmp/

# --- Escape hatch -----------------------------------------------------------
# Templates and examples are the documented, placeholder-only counterparts of the
# machine-local files above. They are exactly what a new contributor needs, so they
# must stay committable even when a rule above would have caught the name.
!*.example
!*.template
!*.sample

# --- Appended 2026-09-01 (arming pass) --------------------------------------
# check-no-pii.sh names FIVE machine-local files in its header; four were already
# covered above, this one was not. It holds real proper nouns (people, projects,
# clients) used as a denylist — precisely the content this repo must never carry.
# Verified with: git check-ignore -v .governance-pii-denylist
.governance-pii-denylist
**/.governance-pii-denylist
